# UI List Pages

## Standard layout
```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Page header (title + actions)                       │
│  KPI band (optional — open incidents, datasets, …)   │
│  Filter bar (search, dropdowns, date range)          │
│  Table / virtualized list                            │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## KPI band
Row of 4 headline numbers above the list. Use `kpi-label` + `kpi-value` classes. Example:
```tsx
<KpiCard label={t('incidents.kpis.open')} value={openCount} />
<KpiCard label={t('incidents.kpis.meanDetect')} value={meanDetect} unit="min" />
```

## Filter bar
- Search input on the left (Cmd-K alternative for module-scoped search).
- Dropdowns for categorical filters (severity, status, engine, dataset).
- Date range picker for time filters.
- "Clear filters" link appears when any filter is active.
- Filters sync to URL search params.

## Table
shadcn/ui `Table` base. Row behaviour:
- Hover: `bg-2` tint (220ms transition).
- Click: navigate to detail page. Entire row is a link (`<tr>` wraps an `<a>` or uses `router.push`).
- No checkboxes in MVP (bulk actions deferred).

### Column patterns
| Content | Component |
|---|---|
| Status | `<StatusDot status={...} />` |
| Verdict / severity | `<Badge variant="pass|warn|fail">` |
| Detector score | `<StatChip metric={slug} value={score} />` |
| Sparkline | `<Spark data={history} />` |
| Timestamp | `<LocalizedDateTime value={ts} format="short" />` |
| Engine | `<EngineGlyph engine={engine} size={14} />` |

## Virtualized list
For large lists (incidents, audit log), use `@tanstack/react-virtual` to virtualise rows. Default page size 50; infinite scroll triggers next page at 80% scroll depth via React Query `useInfiniteQuery`.

## Empty state
When the list is empty (no data yet), show a centred empty-state panel with:
1. A simple icon (lucide, stroke 1.6).
2. A one-line heading.
3. A one-line sub-text.
4. A primary action button if applicable ("Add source", "Create check").

Never show a blank table with column headers and no rows.

## Loading state
Show skeleton rows matching the expected row height while the first page loads. Use `animate-pulse` with `bg-2` color.
